What is PATH?
PATH is an environment variable that tells the shell where to look for executable files (like gcc, ls, etc.).

Print the Current PATH Variable:
echo $PATH

Temporarily Add a Directory to PATH
export PATH=$PATH:/your/new/directory

Permanently Set or Update PATH
You can modify PATH in one of these config files (depending on your shell):

Shell	File
Bash	~/.bashrc or ~/.bash_profile
Zsh	~/.zshrc
Fish	~/.config/fish/config.fish

Add to .bashrc (example):
export PATH=$PATH:/home/user/mytools

Then apply the changes:
source ~/.bashrc

